riscos-risc3d (0.23-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * rol-3d 0.20: contexts that share objects (textures, buffers, programs,
    sync objects), for WebKit's Skia, which draws in several threads with
    a context each. Each context's process also listens on its own
    abstract socket, "rol-3d-<pid>" (the pid goes to Linux3D with the
    memory); a context opened there is a thread in that process, with an
    EGL context in the first one's share group. A context's state is now
    thread-local; the process ends with its last context.
  * A fence made in one context and waited for in another is waited for
    until it reaches its renderer (up to 2 s).
  * "rol-3d-info" answers end ";share" (Linux3D 0.06 asks).
  * Needs RISC OS's side 0.06-1 (RISC3D 0.06, Linux3D 0.06: the PackMan
    package RISC3D) for programs to share; with 0.05-1 everything works as
    before, without sharing.

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.22-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * RISC OS's side moves to PackMan, as on every system: the package RISC3D
    (!RISC3D in !Boot.Resources, with Linux3D), which riscos-harddisc
    1.0.0058-1 installs and PackMan then updates. This package keeps only
    Linux's side: rol-3d and the Mesa pin. It depends on that
    riscos-harddisc.
  * On an upgrade from 0.21-1, dpkg removes 0.21-1's files in !RISC3D, which
    are at the same paths as PackMan's copy: the postinst puts back any that
    are missing, from riscos-harddisc's staged copy, when PackMan's Status
    records RISC3D.
  * The PreDesk.RISC3D start-up file is no longer needed (!Boot.Resources
    loads !RISC3D) and is removed if it is the one this package made.

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.21-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * !RISC3D's !Boot (and !Run) now also load RISC3D, as on native RISC OS:
    programs need nothing in their !Run. The PreDesk.RISC3D file is kept
    (it runs the same !Boot; harmless).

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:00:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.20-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * RISC3D is now !RISC3D in HardDisc4.!Boot.Resources, as on native RISC
    OS: !RISC3D.RISC3D (module 0.04) and !RISC3D.GPU.Linux3D. Its !Boot
    sets RISC3D$Dir and RISC3D$Path, so programs need only
    "RMEnsure RISC3D 0.04 RMLoad RISC3D:RISC3D"; RISC3D 0.04 loads its
    driver from GPU itself. HardDisc4.TestBed.RISC3D goes.
  * The start-up file (PreDesk.RISC3D) now loads RISC3D:RISC3D only; it is
    rewritten if it is still 0.19-1's or earlier (yours if you changed it;
    not made again if you deleted it).
  * Reloading RISC3D now reloads Linux3D from GPU (it used to be left
    unregistered until *RMReInit Linux3D).
  * rol-3d unchanged (0.19).

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.19-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * Mesa from Debian's trixie-backports (ROL's choice, 15 Nov 2026): the
    package carries /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian-backports.sources and
    /etc/apt/preferences.d/riscos-risc3d-mesa (src:mesa pinned at 500 to
    trixie-backports; nothing else follows backports). On first install
    it asks Updates to run apt again (/var/lib/riscos/apt-again), which
    brings the newer Mesa. Removing the package removes both files.
  * rol-3d 0.19: logs Mesa's version; the V3D texture-matrix workaround
    is used only below Mesa 25.2, and a note says how to upgrade.

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:50:00 +0000

riscos-risc3d (0.18-1) rol; urgency=medium

  * rol-3d 0.18: works round a bug in the Pi 4's Mesa (V3D, 25.0.7):
    with lighting on, textures lost their coordinates (TORCS: plain
    yellow car, striped trees, smeared grass). On V3D only, a texture
    matrix left at the identity is given to Mesa with r scaled by the
    float after 1, which takes Mesa's working path; the program's own
    matrices are unchanged. ROL3D_TEXMAT=0 turns it off, =1 on anywhere.

 -- Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:45:00 +0000

